  New Architecture

  PdaNetMonitorService (permanent, regular Service):
  - Foreground service with notification (always visible)
  - Monitors network changes via NetworkCallback
  - Detects PdaNet WiFi (gateway 192.168.49.1)
  - Spawns Tun2HttpVpnService when PdaNet detected
  - If VpnService dies, monitor service detects and respawns it
  - Updates notification: "Waiting for PdaNet..." → "Connected via PdaNet"

  Tun2HttpVpnService (spawned by monitor, VpnService):
  - No foreground service
  - No notification
  - No network monitoring
  - Just establishes VPN tunnel when started
  - Gets torn down by VPN subsystem when network lost → monitor respawns it

  Benefits

  ✅ Notification always visible (from permanent service, not VPN service)
  ✅ VPN subsystem can kill VpnService all it wants - monitor rebuilds it
  ✅ Network monitoring in permanent service (immune to VPN lifecycle)
  ✅ Clean separation: monitor manages lifecycle, VPN just does tunneling

